        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-27T04:31:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Have you tested this ? I fear it may send RemoteException, which in this place would crash the system (and possibly cause a boot loop).\n\nAlso, if it uses INVALID_SUBSCRIPTION_ID, then in systemReady this will lead to the wrong result in updateNotificationsNL – is that fine ?",
      "parentUuid": "4beaf78f_7a331939",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 840,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 840,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "d42a1d765219c77b20cdcec41660ee551cf7b1e7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed49bdfc_4ac1a2b5",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 840,
      "author": {
        "id": 1929200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-01T20:36:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The method call will first try to access a static cache https://source.corp.google.com/android-internal/frameworks/base/telephony/java/android/telephony/SubscriptionManager.java;l\u003d260-264 then it will try to make IPC call, but IIUC if phone process is not up yet, the only effect is that iSub is null at https://source.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/base/telephony/java/android/telephony/SubscriptionManager.java;l\u003d196-197, in that case the default INVALID_SUBSCRIPTION_ID will be returned?\n\nIf INVALID_SUBSCRIPTION_ID is returned, I think it indicates that phone process(either up or not) couldn\u0027t determine a default nor active data subId, then I think data limit/warnings still shouldn\u0027t show, which is not considered wrong in terms of the knowledge of phone process?",
      "parentUuid": "9719a26a_d7e6dda2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 840,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 840,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "d42a1d765219c77b20cdcec41660ee551cf7b1e7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
